Switches a digital output (relay) on the router in response to a Cumulocity IoT
operation, and lets it be toggled locally over the thin-edge.io MQTT bus.

This is an extension for the thin-edge.io platform Router App. It demonstrates
the two integration patterns:

  * A daemon (relay-agent) subscribes to the local MQTT topic relay/<id>/set and
    drives the output. Test it with:  tedge mqtt pub relay/main/set CLOSED
  * Cumulocity custom operations c8y_Relay (single, relayState OPEN/CLOSED) and
    c8y_RelayArray (the RelayArray widget) are registered with the thin-edge.io
    mapper so the relay can be switched from the cloud; the new state is
    reflected into the managed object so the relay widgets update.

Works on ICR routers that expose binary outputs via the ICR-OS "io" command,
including the ICR-1642 (one output, OUT0) and the ICR-44xx family (OUT0/OUT1).
Select the output with MOD_RELAY_OUTPUT, or set MOD_RELAY_PIN for a non-"outN"
pin (e.g. an expansion port).

Install the thin-edge.io platform module first, then this extension. Enable it on
this module's configuration page. See docs/EXTENSION-API.md.
